  "text": "PDF\nUser Guide\nThis User Guide contains information on BIG-IP AS3 and how to install and use it.\nAbout BIG-IP AS3\nThe Application Services 3 Extension uses a\ndeclarative\nmodel, meaning you send a\ndeclaration file using a single Rest API call. This guide gives an overview of\nthe major components of BIG-IP AS3, with references to more information later in this\ndocument.  See\nDocument Revision History\nfor information on document changes.\nUse the following index and/or the Next/Previous buttons and left and right navigation to explore this User Guide.\nNote\nAs of 3.17.0, BIG-IP AS3 provides feature support for LTM, GTM/DNS, APM, AFM, ASM, and PEM modules. Refer to the product documentation for details on the capabilities supported in these modules.\nUser Guide Index\nPrerequisites and Requirements\nBIG-IP AS3 Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)\nComponents\nBIG-IP AS3 Declaration\nBIG-IP AS3 JSON Schema\nWarnings, Notes, & Tips\nWarnings\nNotes and Tips\nKnown Issues\nQuick Start\nQuick start example declaration\nBIG-IP AS3 Best Practices\nArchitecture overview\nBest Practices\nWorkarounds\nHTTP Methods\nPOST\nGET\nDELETE\nPATCH\nAuthentication and Authorization\nBasic Auth\nToken Auth\nDownloading and installing the BIG-IP AS3 package\nDownloading the RPM file\nUploading and installing the BIG-IP AS3 file on the BIG-IP\nChecking for a successful installation\nUninstalling BIG-IP AS3\nUninstalling BIG-IP AS3 from the Configuration utility\nUninstalling BIG-IP AS3 from Postman\nUninstalling BIG-IP AS3 using cURL\nUpgrading BIG-IP versions when BIG-IP AS3 is installed\nComposing a BIG-IP AS3 Declaration\nSample declaration\nComponents of the declaration\nValidating a declaration\nUsing BIG-IP AS3 with BIG-IQ\nRequirements for using BIG-IP AS3 with BIG-IQ\nOther important notes and warnings\nDowngrading BIG-IP AS3 on BIG-IQ\nSettings Endpoint\nAvailable options for the settings endpoint\nUsing serializeFileUploads to upload a large number of certificates\nBurst handling\nBurst handling in BIG-IP AS3 v3.23 and later\nEnabling burst handling in BIG-IP AS3 v3.19 - 3.22\nUnchecked mode\nRisks with using Unchecked mode\nUsing Unchecked mode\nExample of Unchecked mode\nPer-Application Declarations\nPer-application schema for validation\nEnabling/disabling the per-application feature\nExample per-application declaration\nPOSTing a per-application\nUsing GET to view applications\nDeleting a per-application declaration\nAdditional per-application declarations\nExample declarations\nExample 1: Simple HTTP application\nExample 2: HTTPS application\nExample 3: TCP virtual server to ICAP with custom monitor\nExample 4: Calling resources from a URL source\nExample 4a: Using PATCH to add a new server to the pool\nLogging\nTroubleshooting\nBIG-IP AS3 general troubleshooting tips\nTroubleshooting\nPrevious\nNext",
